  "footnote": "NPC Standing Committee, Decision on gradually raising the statutory retirement age, and the State Council Measures, Annexes 1 to 3 (13 September 2024), in force from 1 January 2025",
  "notes": "The policy. On 13 September 2024 the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress adopted the Decision on a gradual rise in the statutory retirement age and approved the State Council's Measures. They took effect on 1 January 2025 and phase in over 15 years. In the law's own terms there are three groups. Male workers go from 60 to 63, and women workers whose original statutory age was 55 go to 58. For both, the age rises by one month for every four birth months. Women workers whose original age was 50 go to 55, one month for every two birth months. The last transitional cohorts of all three groups retire in 2039. The bars are computed from the rules in Annexes 1 to 3: each bar is the largest delay among people retiring by the end of that year. The green bars are the two groups on one month per four, adding two to three months a year and reaching 36 months in 2039. The gold bars are women formerly retiring at 50, adding four months a year and reaching 60. The first two steps, 2025 and 2026, are the treatment dose on the next page. Three other clauses matter for identification. Flexible retirement lets people leave up to three years early, but never before the old statutory age, or stay up to three years longer by agreement with the employer. The minimum contribution period rises by six months a year from 2030 and reaches 20 years in 2039. And Article 7 extends unemployment benefit up to the statutory retirement age for claimants who are within a year of it."
